---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sauna Heater With No Electrician Required | P1 Pellet Sauna Stove"
  description="Learn why the P1 pellet sauna stove is designed for sauna owners who want remote-start heat without a dedicated high-voltage electric sauna heater installation."
>
  <main class="seo-page">
    <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to P1</a>
    <section class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Installation guide</p>
      <h1>A Sauna Heater Built to Avoid Major Electrical Work</h1>
      <p class="lede">Many electric sauna heaters need dedicated wiring, electrical planning, and a contractor visit. The P1 takes a different approach: wood pellet heat with controls that plug into a standard 110V outlet.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why sauna heater electrical requirements matter</h2>
      <p>Electrical installation can be one of the biggest hidden costs in a sauna project. Depending on the heater, panel capacity, distance, permitting, and local code, wiring can add friction before you ever take your first sauna.</p>
      <p>The P1 uses wood pellets as the heat source, so the outlet supports the control system rather than acting as the primary heat source.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What the P1 still needs</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A properly sized sauna room, typically 300 to 500 cubic feet.</li>
        <li>Correct clearances, venting, and floor protection.</li>
        <li>Access to quality dry wood pellets.</li>
        <li>A standard 110V outlet for the controls and remote-start features.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Best-fit use cases</h2>
      <p>The no-electrician advantage is especially useful for backyard saunas, cabin saunas, remodels, and customers who want a wood-fired sauna feel without adding a high-voltage electric heater circuit.</p>
      <a class="cta" href="/#contact">Ask about installation</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .seo-page { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 8rem 1.5rem 4rem; color: var(--text-dark); }
  .back-link { color: var(--text-medium); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
  .hero-copy { margin: 2rem 0 3rem; }
  .eyebrow { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .12em; color: var(--accent-warm); font-weight: 700; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); line-height: .98; margin: .75rem 0 1rem; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); margin: 2.75rem 0 1rem; }
  .lede, p, li { color: var(--text-medium); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .cta { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1rem; padding: .9rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 10px; background: var(--stove-dark); color: white; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; }
</style>
